LogRoom turns a photo of your room into an AI reference score and comments, and keeps a record for each room. Use the calendar and charts to look back on how things change, and build a habit of tidying up a little at a time.

LogRoom is a notebook for progress—not a tool that demands a perfect home.

KEY FEATURES
• Take or choose a photo for each room and get an AI score (reference metrics such as floor, surfaces, and storage)
• Save results as history on your device
• Review past records on a calendar and charts
• Add and reorder rooms
• Export and import your data (ZIP backup when you change phones)
• Switch the display language (Japanese, English, Chinese, Spanish, and more)

GETTING STARTED
Sign in with email, Sign in with Apple / Google when available, or continue as a guest. Open the Score tab, choose a room, and send a photo. Scoring requires an internet connection. There is a daily and monthly limit on how many times you can score.

HOW YOUR DATA IS HANDLED
• Photos you select are sent through our server to Google’s Gemini API for scoring. The service is not designed for us to store your room photos like an album.
• Score history and thumbnails are stored mainly on your device. If you clear the app data, that history cannot be restored—use Export when you need a backup.
• Account information is processed by our auth provider. We may use Google Analytics to understand how the app is used. See the privacy policy in the app and on the web.
• The App Store version may show ads via Google AdMob.

ABOUT AI SCORING
Scores and comments are AI reference information only. We do not guarantee accuracy or completeness. Decisions about safety (fire, tripping hazards, hygiene, and so on) are yours, or a qualified professional’s.

AGE
LogRoom is not directed to children under 13 (or under the age required where you live).

CONTACT
Use the in-app contact form or the Support URL on this listing.

